course: dictionary
lesson: 6138
title: The mile
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mile is a unit of distance, a way of measuring how far something is. Walking one mile takes about 20 minutes. One mile is 1760 yards, or 5280 feet.
explain: «Sara walked a million miles round the shops.» Nobody walks a million miles in one trip! Here «miles» means a very long way, so Sara must be very tired.
explain: Look at the words next to mile to find its meaning. «Miles per hour» tells you a speed, and «miles away» tells you how far off something is.
fact: A mile is a unit of distance.
fact: One mile is 1760 yards, or 5280 feet.
fact: Walking one mile takes about 20 minutes.
fact: «Miles» can mean a very long way, as in «miles from home».
fact: Sound travels about 1 mile in 5 seconds, so counting from flash to bang tells you how far away lightning is.
exercise: How many yards are in one mile? | 880 | 100 | 5280 | *1760
exercise: «Sara walked a million miles round the shops.» What does miles mean here? | *A very long way, so she must be tired | Exactly one million miles, measured with a map | Sara's shoe size | A type of bus ticket
exercise: Which phrase tells you a speed? | A mile of road | *Miles per hour | Miles away | The extra mile
test: Sound travels about 1 mile in how many seconds? | *5 seconds | 60 seconds | 1 second | 20 seconds
test: Which countries use miles per hour? | *The USA and the UK | Canada and Australia | Ireland and New Zealand | France and Spain
exam: Mum says, «That's thousands of miles away, love.» What does this tell you? | It is in the next street | It is one mile from the shops | *It is very far away | It is a short walk away
